**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-284 @bug @delivery @check-provenance
Feature: Resolve missing required-check event provenance
  As a developer using exact-head delivery
  I want aggregate required checks bound to authoritative Actions runs
  So that valid pull-request checks pass without trusting unknown provenance

  Scenario: Missing event resolves from an exact-head pull-request run
    Given a successful required check has no event
    And its link names an Actions run
    And the run event is "pull_request"
    And the run head SHA equals the PR head
    When delivery builds the PR snapshot
    Then the check event is "pull_request"
    And existing delivery classification may accept it

  Scenario Outline: Unsafe run evidence remains rejected
    Given a required check has no event
    And run resolution produces <condition>
    When delivery classifies the check
    Then it cannot satisfy pull-request provenance
    And delivery does not merge

    Examples:
      | condition                  |
      | a push event               |
      | a merge_group event        |
      | an empty event             |
      | an unknown event           |
      | a mismatched head SHA      |
      | a malformed Actions link   |
      | an unreadable run          |

  Scenario: Explicit event is preserved
    Given a required check already reports event "pull_request"
    When delivery builds the PR snapshot
    Then it performs no run lookup for that check
    And preserves the explicit event

  Scenario: Shared run lookup is cached
    Given multiple missing-event checks link to the same Actions run
    When delivery builds one PR snapshot
    Then it resolves that run exactly once
    And applies the exact-head event result consistently
